        "original_id": "8e5b9bb1-afef-5a40-9415-9ad387428a6d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Bossiaea, Ferraria, Platylobium\n- Taxonomy: Fabaceae, Iridaceae, Mirbelioids, genera, species\n- People: James Edward Smith\n- Places: Australia, tropical Africa, southern Africa\n\nFacts:\n- Bossiaea is a genus in the pea family Fabaceae with about 70 species native to Australia.\n- Ferraria is a genus of monocotyledonous flowering plants in the family Iridaceae native to tropical and southern Africa.\n- James Edward Smith first described the genus Platylobium.\n- Platylobium is closely allied to Bossiaea within the Mirbelioids.",
